  {
    "id": 46,
    "user": "Lauren Lawrence",
    "role": "assistant",
    "text": "After reading this whole section, Im not sure what the takeaways are. I understand you are studying the impacts of gender on virtual assistants but what are you doing differently from previous works? What are you building on top of from these previous studies? What have you learnt in your literature search/review that informs your decisions now? Who does this impact? How are you going to collect 30 participants? What if you cannot? All of these feel very unanswered to me and perhaps it can be contributed to how your expose has not been divided into digestible sections, making it hard for me to follow your arguments. Without any division to blocks of text, it gets very repetitive and tedious to read. Its important to keep your reader's attention and its very hard when there is just 1 big block of text without any division of what part of the argument we're in now. Atleast when it comes to published works in CS, scientific publications are always divided into blocks by headers within sections",
